# The automation repo, checked out here by 05 - remediate a PR. It is a nested
# git repository, so an unignored `git add -A` records it as a gitlink rather
# than as files — see the SCRATCH comment in .github/workflows/remediate.yml.
# This rule is also why that step's `git add` must not name `.automation`: an
# ignored path named in a pathspec makes `git add` exit 1 instead of skipping it.
.automation/
